        "year": 2018,
        "venue": "Computational Reading Symposium",
        "abstract": "This field guide defines the ego citation neighborhood: a center paper, its references, papers that cite it, and provider-selected recommendations. We argue that bounded samples should be labeled as samples, that citation direction must come from observed provider edges, and that recommendation links should be visually distinct from citations.",
